Description: Drop the timed register-protection tests
 They slept inside actions and bounded the total wall-clock time to within
 20%, which loaded builders overshoot (3777 ms against a 3600 ms limit on an
 OBS Ubuntu 22.04 aarch64 build). Telling serialization from parallelism
 without timing would mean showing that nothing else blocks two actions,
 which no deterministic test can.
Author: Bryan Richter <b@chreekat.net>
Forwarded: not-needed
